WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:05.440
In the case, In re Prudential Insurance&nbsp;
Company sales practices litigation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.720
we'll see what factors courts should evaluate&nbsp;
when determining whether a proposed class&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:15.280
action settlement is fair and reasonable.
 
Eight million Prudential insurance company&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:20.040
policyholders sued Prudential, claiming&nbsp;
that Prudential's sales force engaged in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:25.640
fraudulent and misleading sales practices.
 
After all the parties completed extensive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:30.400
discovery and the policyholders filed&nbsp;
various motions and amended complaints,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.840
the class of policyholders and Prudential&nbsp;
entered into a settlement agreement. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:39.440
terms of the settlement agreement proposed a&nbsp;
remediation scheme that allowed class members&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:43.720
to either pursue their claims through an&nbsp;
alternate dispute resolution procedure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:50.840
known as ADR or elect for basic claim relief.&nbsp;
Under ADR, a class member who believed that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:54.920
or she had been misled by Prudential&nbsp;
Salesforce would submit a claim that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.920 --> 00:01:00.760
would be reviewed in a four tier review process.
 
The review process included reviews by Prudential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:05.480
employees and independent evaluators.
 
Under the basic claim relief, a class&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:09.480
member could obtain relief without&nbsp;
showing Prudential's liability.
 &nbsp;

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:14.640
The proposed settlement agreement was&nbsp;
not capped by a specific dollar amount.
 &nbsp;

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:19.320
The district court certified the class and&nbsp;
approved the settlement. Three hundred class&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:23.400
members objected to the settlement, and a&nbsp;
class member appealed the district court's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:29.920
approval of the settlement agreement to the United&nbsp;
States Court of Appeals for the third circuit.

